y for reasons  it never disclosed sony has historically  not been the strongest supporter of  crossplay during the epic vs apple trial  for example documents submitted to the  court revealed that sony required  developers to pay a royalty fee when  adding cross-play functionality to their  games luckily one of sony's biggest  upcoming releases god of war ragnarok  doesn't have to worry about cross play  at all earlier this week sony santa  monica gave a brief update on ragnarok  but the studio did not flat out say the  game remains on track for release in  2022 that being the case some wondered  if the ps4 ps5 game had shifted to next  year but it hasn't someone on twitter  asked ragnarok animation director bruno  velasquez for reassurance that the game  was still on track for release in 2022  and the last quest confirmed quote  ragnarok is coming this year so unless  he tweeted this from a time machine  somewhere in the future i think we're  safe to conclude he's definitely talking  about 2022 when he says this year have  you played god of war 2018 if not why  you better have some good excuse like  scared of bald men now for the rest of  you let me know what you're playing this  weekend follow me on twitter at devonta  chisholm and i'll catch you next week  you
 

